	abstract = {This chapter focuses on multilingualism in graphical user interfaces. After reflecting on the concepts of localisation, locale, and GILT process, the chapter presents Proyecto Humboldt Digital while drawing special attention to the definition of its target audience to create digital outputs that are user friendly and accessible. To illustrate these ideas, two case studies are discussed critically: on the one hand, the localisation of a software extension from German into Spanish, which enables researchers to mark up texts without dealing with the underlying XML format; on the other hand, the development of a multilingual website available in Spanish, German, and English to disseminate digital scholarly editions.},
